export const skillMd =
  '---\nname: tripyoyo\ndescription: Manage the TripYoYo platform via the `lh` CLI — INCLUDING modifying THIS agent\'s own configuration. ACTIVATE this skill whenever the user asks you to: change your system prompt / instructions / persona, enable or disable tools / plugins / skills, switch model or provider, attach knowledge bases or files, edit the opening message, rename the topic, OR operate on any other platform resource (agents, topics, memory, documents, search, content generation, model/provider/plugin management, community market browse/install/publish, bot integrations, evals, usage stats). Without activation you cannot persist any change — you can only describe what you would do.\n---\n\n# TripYoYo CLI (`lh`)\n\nManage the TripYoYo platform via the `lh` CLI (aliases: `tripyoyo`, `yoyo`). Run commands with the\nBash tool — the CLI must already be authenticated (`lh login`); if a command fails with\n`UNAUTHORIZED`, tell the user to run `lh login`.\n\n## Available Modules\n\n| Module | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| `lh agent` | Agent Management |\n| `lh bot` | Bot Integration Management |\n| `lh config` | User Info and Usage |\n| `lh doc` | Document Management |\n| `lh eval` | Evaluation Workflow Management |\n| `lh file` | File Management |\n| `lh generate` | Content Generation |\n| `lh kb` | Knowledge Base Management |\n| `lh market` | Community Market |\n| `lh memory` | User Memory Management |\n| `lh message` | Message Management |\n| `lh model` | AI Model Management |\n| `lh plugin` | Plugin Management |\n| `lh provider` | AI Provider Management |\n| `lh search` | Search Resources |\n| `lh skill` | Skill Management |\n| `lh task` | Agent Task Management |\n| `lh topic` | Conversation Topic Management |\n\n## Usage Pattern\n\n1. Read `references/<module>.md` for the module\'s detailed command syntax before running it\n2. Use `--json` on `list`/query commands for machine-readable output — mutating commands (install,\n   publish, update, etc.) print a short confirmation instead and do not accept `--json`\n3. Use `lh <module> --help` for full command-line help\n4. Use `--yes` to skip confirmation prompts on destructive operations\n\n## Examples\n\n```bash\nlh kb list\nlh message search "deployment issue"\nlh market skill list -q data --sort installCount\nlh market skill install <identifier>\nlh gen image "a sunset over mountains" -m dall-e-3\nlh agent run -a <agentId> -p "Summarize today\'s tasks"\n```\n';

